    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d677">

                <pb facs="0823" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/694</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-30T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.28 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6848. Your 5222, undated [<hi rendition="#italic">July 28, 5 p.m.</hi>]. No. The
                    reference to Stockholm conference is correct, for that is where it is to be
                    held. Information contained in my 6826, July 27, 1 p.m., obtained from Mr.
                    Arthur Henderson. No definite decision has yet been arrived at by British
                    Government as to the attitude which will be finally adopted towards this
                    conference. Shall keep you informed of developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
